{"path":"io/basic_streambuf/pbump","title":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::pbump","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>pbump","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pbump","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Repositions the put pointer (pptr()) by count characters, where count may be positive or negative. No checks are done for moving the pointer outside the put area [pbase(), epptr()).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> pbump<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Repositions the <i>put pointer</i> (<span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pptr\">pptr()</a></span>) by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> characters, where <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> may be positive or negative. No checks are done for moving the pointer outside the put area <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pbase<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">epptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>)</code></span>.\n</p><p>If the pointer is advanced and then <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/overflow\">overflow()</a></span> is called to flush the put area to the associated character sequence, the effect is that extra <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> characters with undefined values are output.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> count\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> number to add to the put pointer\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Because this function takes an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span></code>, it cannot manipulate buffers larger than <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> characters (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue255\" data-external=\"1\">LWG issue 255</a>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;fstream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> showput_streambuf <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_filebuf\"><span class=\"kw1742\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filebuf</span></span></a>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filebuf</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">pbump</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// expose protected</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> showput<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pbase<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, pptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    showput_streambuf mybuf<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    mybuf.<span class=\"me1\">open</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"test.txt\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1692\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">out</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\"><span class=\"kw1746\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostream</span></span></a> str<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>mybuf<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    str <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"This is a test\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/flush\"><span class=\"kw1807\">std::<span class=\"me2\">flush</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"1234\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"The put area contains: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> mybuf.<span class=\"me1\">showput</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    mybuf.<span class=\"me1\">pbump</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">10</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"after pbump(10), it contains \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> mybuf.<span class=\"me1\">showput</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>The put area contains: 1234\nafter pbump(10), it contains 1234 is a test</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/gbump\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>gbump</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  advances the next pointer in the input sequence <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(protected member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_streambuf","title":"std::basic_streambuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::pbump","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Repositions the put pointer (pptr()) by count characters, where count may be positive or negative."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"count"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Because this function takes an int, it cannot manipulate buffers larger than std::numeric_limits<int>::max() characters (LWG issue 255)."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"gbump","note":"advances the next pointer in the input sequence"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":194,"codeBlockCount":2}
